WEBVTT

00:00:06.042 --> 00:00:07.667
Join Dance Girls group chat?
YES

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:09.499
u got a lilypad!!!

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:10.791
YES!

00:00:10.792 --> 00:00:13.416
are u free on sat?

00:00:13.417 --> 00:00:14.874
- [Bonnie screams]
- [coughs]

00:00:14.875 --> 00:00:15.957
- Mom! Dad!
- Bonnie?

00:00:15.958 --> 00:00:17.457
What? [stammers] What's wrong?

00:00:17.458 --> 00:00:18.374
Chelsea from dance class

00:00:18.375 --> 00:00:19.957
invited me to a sleepover this weekend.

00:00:19.958 --> 00:00:22.000
Can I go? Can I go? Can I go?

00:00:22.833 --> 00:00:24.124
Please!

00:00:24.125 --> 00:00:26.041
Well, uh, all right.

00:00:26.042 --> 00:00:28.999
As long as we talk to Chelsea's parents,

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.416
I guess it's okay.

00:00:30.417 --> 00:00:32.416
Yay! Yes!

00:00:32.417 --> 00:00:34.458
[Dad] Come on, everybody. Let's eat.

00:00:37.875 --> 00:00:39.874
Yeah, I got dibs on behind the dresser.

00:00:39.875 --> 00:00:41.166
Should buy me a few years.

00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:43.499
Ah! Extinction. Not again.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.082
- Called it.
- Don't get me started.

00:00:45.083 --> 00:00:48.332
Now, look. Our time ain't over yet.
Bonnie still loves us.

00:00:48.333 --> 00:00:49.874
- [Dolly] Really?
- [Jessie] She does.

00:00:49.875 --> 00:00:52.583
Sure. Whatever you say, Sheriff.

00:00:54.458 --> 00:00:56.083
It's just a phase.

00:00:58.375 --> 00:00:59.624
[sighs]

00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:01.708
[♪ sentimental music playing]

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:14.750
[♪ marching music playing]

00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:28.042
[static crackling]

00:01:29.875 --> 00:01:30.875
[sighs]

00:01:32.083 --> 00:01:35.207
[beeping]

00:01:35.208 --> 00:01:37.166
'Ello? Caboom here. Over.

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:39.832
- [Jessie] <i>Oh! Duke.</i>
- Hey there, Red.

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:41.957
- Long time.
<i>- Hey. Um...</i>

00:01:41.958 --> 00:01:43.917
<i>- Is Woody there?</i>
- Please hold.

00:01:48.417 --> 00:01:50.249
[exclaims] Hey, cowboy!

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:51.999
Pump the brakes, Duke, he's mid-rescue.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.249
Bad squirrel! No! Yeah, bad!

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:56.499
- Evil squirrel! No!
- Okay, now, Mr. Nutcase.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.207
- Doctor. Doctor.
- Okay, Dr. Nutcase.

00:01:59.208 --> 00:02:02.124
On three, you're going to unstick yourself

00:02:02.125 --> 00:02:03.666
- and drop into my arms.
- [sobbing]

00:02:03.667 --> 00:02:06.416
What's the point? It's over for toys.

00:02:06.417 --> 00:02:09.957
The screens have won, and now
the squirrel's gonna eat me!

00:02:09.958 --> 00:02:11.166
You guys ready?

00:02:11.167 --> 00:02:12.957
Just one text, ping,

00:02:12.958 --> 00:02:14.916
and Trevor totally forgot
I was stuck in the tree.

00:02:14.917 --> 00:02:16.249
[crying] We're doomed!

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:20.124
Okay, one, two...

00:02:20.125 --> 00:02:21.332
I give up!

00:02:21.333 --> 00:02:22.625
[shouts] Three, three!

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.291
I got you. I got you.

00:02:26.292 --> 00:02:27.832
[Dr. Nutcase sobbing]

00:02:27.833 --> 00:02:31.750
- Okay. It's okay. I got you.
- Let me go! I'm yucky.

00:02:32.958 --> 00:02:35.624
- [Woody] <i>Hello, Jessie? Hello?</i>
- [gasps] Woody!

00:02:35.625 --> 00:02:37.457
Jessie, hey. What's going on?

00:02:37.458 --> 00:02:39.124
- Curse technology!
- Hey, quiet down.

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:41.541
[Dr. Nutcase] <i>We're all just landfill now.</i>

00:02:41.542 --> 00:02:44.874
Woody, is it as bad out there
for toys as they say it is?

00:02:44.875 --> 00:02:46.707
- Beware the machines!
- Just let go!

00:02:46.708 --> 00:02:48.124
Yeah. Yeah, it's bad.

00:02:48.125 --> 00:02:50.457
We're finding
more abandoned toys each day.

00:02:50.458 --> 00:02:52.041
Why? Are you guys okay?

00:02:52.042 --> 00:02:55.666
Not really. Tech's invaded our house too.

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:56.582
[Woody] <i>Oh, no.</i>

00:02:56.583 --> 00:02:58.374
Yeah, her name's Lilypad.

00:02:58.375 --> 00:03:00.999
Looks like a frog,
but really, she's a leech,

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.332
<i>sucking up all of Bonnie's attention.</i>

00:03:03.333 --> 00:03:06.540
<i>Making her stare at her screen all day.</i>

00:03:06.541 --> 00:03:08.999
<i>There's got to be some way to stop it.</i>

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.040
[stammers] I don't know, Jessie. Uh...

00:03:11.041 --> 00:03:14.165
Toys are for play, but tech is...

00:03:14.166 --> 00:03:16.332
<i>it's for everything.</i>

00:03:16.333 --> 00:03:17.583
[sighs]

00:03:19.125 --> 00:03:21.999
You remember my first kid, Emily?

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:25.540
The one I told you about who gave me away.

00:03:25.541 --> 00:03:27.290
[Woody] <i>Course I do, yeah.</i>

00:03:27.291 --> 00:03:30.208
It feels like that all over again.

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:32.874
<i>First we were playing...</i>

00:03:32.875 --> 00:03:33.957
[Emily laughs]

00:03:33.958 --> 00:03:36.041
<i>...and then the world started changing.</i>

00:03:36.042 --> 00:03:38.207
[laughs] I know.

00:03:38.208 --> 00:03:40.333
[Jessie] <i>Emily changed and then...</i>

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:42.332
<i>just like that...</i>

00:03:42.333 --> 00:03:43.374
DONATIONS

00:03:43.375 --> 00:03:45.542
<i>...my time with her was over.</i>

00:03:46.958 --> 00:03:50.292
Now I'm losing Bonnie to this device.

00:03:51.625 --> 00:03:53.083
Is it me?

00:03:53.583 --> 00:03:56.124
Am I just no good at being a toy?

00:03:56.125 --> 00:03:58.166
[Woody] <i>Jessie, you're a good toy.</i>

00:03:58.167 --> 00:04:00.583
- I don't know.
- [Woody] <i>Jessie.</i>

00:04:02.833 --> 00:04:03.917
[Bullseye grunts]

00:04:04.917 --> 00:04:07.707
[inhales sharply] Okay.
Jessie... [clears throat]

00:04:07.708 --> 00:04:10.791
No, Sheriff... Sheriff Jessie,
I appreciate this promotion,

00:04:10.792 --> 00:04:12.624
but what I'd really like to promote...

00:04:12.625 --> 00:04:14.499
No, that is so stupid.

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:15.958
[Bullseye sniffing]

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:19.707
But she got Bonnie invited
to a sleepover in seconds.

00:04:19.708 --> 00:04:22.874
[Woody] <i>Jessie, you know
Bonnie better than anyone.</i>

00:04:22.875 --> 00:04:24.458
<i>What does your gut say?</i>

00:04:30.542 --> 00:04:32.666
- That it can't be that easy.
- [Woody] <i>Mm-hmm.</i>

00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:33.749
Bonnie won't click

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:35.166
- with just anyone.
<i>- Exactly.</i>

00:04:35.167 --> 00:04:37.749
She needs to actually meet these girls.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:41.667
She's not like most kids.
Bonnie plays different. She...

00:04:43.833 --> 00:04:45.333
She needs to play.

00:04:45.833 --> 00:04:47.749
- [Woody] <i>Jessie?</i>
- You're right, Woody.

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:49.124
Toys are for play.

00:04:49.125 --> 00:04:52.041
<i>And play is how
she'll find the right friend.</i>

00:04:52.042 --> 00:04:52.957
Okay.

00:04:52.958 --> 00:04:55.291
The age of toys may be over,

00:04:55.292 --> 00:04:58.291
but I'm gonna do something
useful before I go.

00:04:58.292 --> 00:04:59.791
I'm going to that sleepover,

00:04:59.792 --> 00:05:02.541
and making a real friend for Bonnie.

00:05:02.542 --> 00:05:04.541
- Jessie, are you okay?
- [gasps] Buzz!

00:05:04.542 --> 00:05:06.166
- Jessie? Jessie!
- [static on radio]

00:05:06.167 --> 00:05:07.582
What do you think you're doing?

00:05:07.583 --> 00:05:09.707
What are you doing?
I assumed you needed backup.

00:05:09.708 --> 00:05:10.832
No! I don't...

00:05:10.833 --> 00:05:13.582
<i>Need backup, Deputy.</i>

00:05:13.583 --> 00:05:14.667
[gasps]

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:17.374
- [whispers] What happened?
- Why are we whispering?

00:05:17.375 --> 00:05:18.457
- He's finally asleep.
- [snoring]

00:05:18.458 --> 00:05:19.541
So what's wrong?

00:05:19.542 --> 00:05:21.957
I don't know, but you heard Jessie.

00:05:21.958 --> 00:05:23.541
She needs a deputy.

00:05:23.542 --> 00:05:24.791
[screams] Machines!

00:05:24.792 --> 00:05:26.791
- Jessie.
- Yeah, what is it?

00:05:26.792 --> 00:05:27.875
Uh...

00:05:29.667 --> 00:05:31.666
[stammers] You know...
Never mind. Never mind.

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:33.957
If you need anything,
I'm here. At your service.

00:05:33.958 --> 00:05:35.667
Okay. Thanks.

00:05:36.167 --> 00:05:38.499
Come on, Bullseye.
I'm gonna need your help.

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:39.916
[Bullseye whinnies]

00:05:39.917 --> 00:05:41.292
[Buzz sighs]

00:05:46.667 --> 00:05:49.167
[♪ adventurous music playing]

00:05:59.833 --> 00:06:02.207
We can't see the stars, Buzz.
Too much fog.

00:06:02.208 --> 00:06:05.625
Hmm. We need to find higher ground.

00:06:06.125 --> 00:06:08.625
- [gasps]
- [all beeping]

00:06:17.333 --> 00:06:19.333
[♪ dramatic music playing]

